---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How many calories in the DQ Chicken Strip Basket?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The 4-Piece has approximately 1,000 calories including fries and Texas toast. The 6-Piece has approximately 1,380 calories. Calorie count varies slightly depending on your dipping sauce choice."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the best dipping sauce for DQ chicken strips?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Country Gravy is the traditional and most popular pairing. Ranch is a close second. For something bolder, try the FlameThrower Sauced Basket which has spicy sauce tossed directly onto the strips."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---
<Layout title="Dairy Queen Chicken Strip Basket Menu & Prices 2026" description="DQ Chicken Strip Basket menu with 2026 prices. 4-Piece $9.99, 6-Piece $13.49. Honey BBQ, Parmesan Garlic, FlameThrower.">
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />


<Breadcrumbs items={[{"name": "Home", "href": "/"}, {"name": "Menu", "href": "/categories"}, {"name": "DQ Chicken Strip Baskets 2026"}]} />

<section class="hero">
<div class="container">
<div class="hero-content">
<span class="hero-eyebrow">Chicken strips · Fries · Texas toast · Gravy</span>
<h1>Dairy Queen Chicken Strip Basket Menu With Prices</h1>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section"><div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <p class="lead"><strong>A 4-piece Chicken Strip Basket at Dairy Queen costs about $9.99, and a 6-piece about $13.49.</strong> Each basket comes with fries, Texas toast and a dipping sauce; most people choose the warm country gravy. The strips are whole pieces of chicken breast, breaded and fried.</p>
    <p>Here are all the chicken strip options with prices and calories. For a full comparison, see our <a href="/blog/dq-chicken-strip-baskets-review">4-piece vs 6-piece basket review</a>. On a budget? The <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a> includes three strips, fries, a drink and a sundae.</p>


    <h2>Chicken Strip Basket Menu — All Options &amp; Prices</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Price</th><th>Approx. Calories</th><th>Includes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/chicken-strip-basket-4pc">4-Piece Chicken Strip Basket</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$9.99</td><td>~1,000</td><td>4 strips, fries, Texas toast, dipping sauce</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/chicken-strip-basket-6pc">6-Piece Chicken Strip Basket</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$13.49</td><td>~1,380</td><td>6 strips, fries, Texas toast, dipping sauce</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/honey-bbq-chicken-strip-basket">Honey BBQ Basket (4-Pc)</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$10.49</td><td>~1,100</td><td>Strips tossed in honey BBQ sauce, fries, Texas toast</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Parmesan Garlic Basket (4-Pc)</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$10.49</td><td>~1,080</td><td>Strips tossed in Parmesan garlic sauce, fries, Texas toast</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>FlameThrower® Basket (4-Pc)</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$10.49</td><td>~940</td><td>Strips with FlameThrower sauce, fries, Texas toast</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/2pc-chicken-strips">2-Piece Chicken Strips (snack)</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>~280</td><td>Two strips only, no sides</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2>Dipping Sauce Options</h2>
    <p>Every basket comes with one dipping sauce of your choice. Available options at most locations:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Country Gravy</strong> — The classic DQ pairing. Creamy white gravy with a savory, slightly peppery flavor. The most popular choice by far.</li>
      <li><strong>Ranch</strong> — The second most popular. Cool and creamy, balances the crispy chicken well.</li>
      <li><strong>Honey Mustard</strong> — Sweet and tangy, a good option if you want something lighter than gravy.</li>
      <li><strong>BBQ Sauce</strong> — Smoky and sweet, pairs particularly well with the plain 4-Piece basket.</li>
      <li><strong>Sweet &amp; Sour</strong> — A lighter, fruit-forward option.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><em>Sauced Baskets (Honey BBQ, Parmesan Garlic, FlameThrower) have the sauce tossed onto the strips themselves. You still receive a dipping sauce on the side.</em></p>

    <h2>4-piece or 6-piece: which to order</h2>
    <p>The 4-Piece ($9.99) is the standard individual meal. It comes with fries and Texas toast and has approximately 1,000 calories total — a complete, satisfying lunch or dinner. The 6-Piece ($13.49) adds two more strips and approximately 380 extra calories. The 6-Piece is the right call if you are very hungry, want to share a couple of strips, or want leftovers.</p>
    <p>The sauced basket options (Honey BBQ, Parmesan Garlic, FlameThrower) cost $10.49 for the 4-Piece — a $0.50 premium for the pre-tossed sauce. If you want flavor in every bite rather than just dipping, the sauced version is worth the small upcharge.</p>

